course: dictionary
lesson: 4148
title: Glucose, the body's fuel
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Glucose is a kind of sugar. Your body uses it for energy, and your blood carries it to every cell. «Blood glucose» means the amount of glucose in your blood.
explain: «Too little sugar is a hypo» tells you a hypo is a low sugar level. The next part says fast sugar like juice or glucose tablets fixes it. So the clues show that glucose is a quick fix when sugar is too low.
explain: Glucose is a science word, so the topic gives you clues too: food, plants and health. Ask yourself what would fit here, then put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Glucose is a kind of sugar that your body uses for energy.
fact: Your blood carries glucose to all your cells.
fact: Plants make glucose from sunlight, water and carbon dioxide.
fact: «Glucose tablets» are sold to help when blood sugar is too low.
fact: «A continuous glucose monitor» measures sugar every few minutes and sends the reading to a phone.
exercise: «A hypo is treated with fast sugar such as glucose tablets or juice.» What is glucose? | A part of the blood that fights germs | *A kind of sugar your body uses for energy | A type of bone | A fizzy drink with no sugar at all
exercise: Plants make glucose. What do they use to make it? | *Sunlight, water and carbon dioxide | Rocks and sand | Sweets and fizzy drinks | A tall tree and a pot of soil
exercise: «Too little sugar is a hypo.» What does hypo mean here? | A type of sweet | *Too little sugar | Too much sugar | A healthy meal
test: People with diabetes check their «blood glucose». Why? | To measure how tall they are | To count their steps | To check the weather | *To see how much sugar is in their blood
test: «A hypo is treated with glucose tablets, then the level is checked again in 15 minutes.» What is checked after 15 minutes? | Tomorrow's weather | The length of a walk | The colour of the sky | *The blood sugar level
exam: «Blood glucose» in a text about diabetes most likely means | How loud a voice is | The number of people in a family | *The amount of glucose in the blood | How quickly a runner moves
